  "worked_solution": "A vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ with a simply connected domain $D\u2286{R}^{2}$ has a stream function $\u03c8(x,y)$ if and only if\n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202x}+\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202y}=0.\n$$\n\nNote that $F(x,y)=2{x}^{2}y\\,i-2x{y}^{2}\\,j$ is a vector field with simply connected domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P(x,y)=2{x}^{2}y$ and $Q(x,y)=-2x{y}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202x}=4xy,\\,\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202y} & =-4xy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $F$ has a stream function, since\n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202x}+\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202y}=4xy+(-4xy)=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we find a stream function. A function $\u03c8(x,y)$ is a stream function of the vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ if \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{\u2202\u03c8}{\u2202y},\\,Q=-\\frac{\u2202\u03c8}{\u2202x}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202\u03c8}{\u2202y}=2{x}^{2}y,\\,\\frac{\u2202\u03c8}{\u2202x}=2x{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIntegrating these equations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\u03c8(x,y)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}+f(x),\\,\u03c8(x,y)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}+g(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are arbitrary functions. Finally, setting $f=g=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\u03c8(x,y)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}=(xy)^{2}.\n$$",
